(*!
<summary>Beckhoff EL3413/EL3433 bidirectional auxiliary measurement channel.</summary>
<description>
Combines auxiliary TxPDO 0x1A03 and selector RxPDO 0x1603 in the represented default process image.
Input status and selector acknowledgements determine when Value can be interpreted for the requested quantity.
This interface is not present in EL3403. Link fields individually; this is not a packed EtherCAT packet.
Use one owner task; externally synchronize other access. Copies store data without creating hardware links.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE POWER_MEASUREMENT_AUXILIARY_CHANNEL :
STRUCT
	In : POWER_MEASUREMENT_AUXILIARY_INPUT_CHANNEL;
	Out : POWER_MEASUREMENT_AUXILIARY_OUTPUT_CHANNEL;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
